values('project-programme-portfolio-03','project-programme-portfolio',1,'1.4','Why does an organisation use project management rather than simply letting each specialist complete their own tasks independently?','[{"id":"a","text":"To ensure that the project manager performs every technical task."},{"id":"b","text":"To replace all specialist judgement with a fixed schedule."},{"id":"c","text":"To remove the need to make trade-offs."},{"id":"d","text":"To coordinate work and control delivery towards agreed objectives."}]'::jsonb,'d','Project management integrates specialist contributions and handles constraints, dependencies and uncertainty. Specialists still provide expertise, and trade-offs still need decisions. A schedule supports this work but does not replace it.')
