values('business-case-01','business-case',1,'4.4','A large forecast increase in support costs appears after project approval. How should the business case be treated?','[{"id":"a","text":"Ignore the increase because approval makes the case permanent."},{"id":"b","text":"Remove the costs from reporting to protect the original figures."},{"id":"c","text":"Replace it with a task list."},{"id":"d","text":"Update the evidence so the sponsor can reassess continuing justification."}]'::jsonb,'d','A business case is maintained as assumptions and forecasts change. Approval does not make the investment permanently worthwhile. Omitting costs hides evidence, and a task list does not answer whether the investment is justified.')
