values('resource-scheduling-03','resource-scheduling',1,'6.6','Which description best fits a procurement strategy?','[{"id":"a","text":"The order in which a report’s pages are printed."},{"id":"b","text":"An approach to obtaining required goods/services, including sourcing, contracting and risk/timing choices."},{"id":"c","text":"A guarantee to select the lowest price in every case."},{"id":"d","text":"A list of completed lesson titles."}]'::jsonb,'b','Procurement strategy addresses how the required supply will be obtained and managed. Price is one consideration, alongside capability, contracts, timing and risk. A printing sequence or unrelated list is not a sourcing approach.')
