values('information-and-reporting-03','information-and-reporting',1,'4.11','Why should reports distinguish actual performance from forecast performance?','[{"id":"a","text":"Because forecasts must never change."},{"id":"b","text":"Because actual spending proves the final cost automatically."},{"id":"c","text":"Because recipients should never question assumptions."},{"id":"d","text":"Because what has happened and what is now expected answer different control questions."}]'::jsonb,'d','Actuals describe performance to a reporting date; forecasts describe the expected future position. Both are useful and neither removes the need to examine assumptions, remaining work or the authorised baseline.')
