values('leadership-and-teamwork-03','leadership-and-teamwork',1,'10.2','Which manager behaviour is most likely to support team performance?','[{"id":"a","text":"Clarify shared goals, invite early concerns and remove obstacles."},{"id":"b","text":"Reward silence about emerging problems."},{"id":"c","text":"Assume formal authority guarantees commitment."},{"id":"d","text":"Use the same support approach regardless of experience or circumstances."}]'::jsonb,'a','Clear direction, constructive feedback and practical support help people contribute. Suppressing concerns or relying solely on authority can hide problems. Leadership should respond to the situation and team needs.')
